{"id":"mahabharata-13-027","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":27,"title":"सप्तविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 27 · The glory of the Ganga","summary":{"en":"Bhishma tells of a gleaner brahmin, learned and peaceful, who asked a siddha about the Ganga, and the siddha tells of her glory. He says that all beings who are sprinkled with her waters reach perfect peace, and that Shiva bore her falling from heaven on his head.","kn":"ಬುದ್ಧಿವಂತ, ಶಾಂತ ಉಂಛವೃತ್ತಿಯ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಸಿದ್ಧನನ್ನು ಗಂಗೆಯ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ ಸಿದ್ಧ ಅವಳ ಮಹಿಮೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆಕೆಯ ನೀರು ಸಿಂಪಡಿಸಿಕೊಂಡ ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳು ಪರಮ ತೃಪ್ತಿ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತವೆ; ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಿಂದ ಬೀಳುವ ಗಂಗೆಯನ್ನು ಶಿವ ತಲೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಧರಿಸಿದ.","hi":"भीष्म विद्वान और शान्त उञ्छवृत्ति ब्राह्मण की कथा कहते हैं जिसने सिद्ध से गंगा के बारे में पूछा और सिद्ध ने उसकी महिमा बताई। वे कहते हैं कि उसके जल से सिंचे सब प्राणी परम तृप्ति पाते हैं और स्वर्ग से गिरती गंगा को शिव ने सिर पर धारण किया।","te":"విద్వాంసుడు, శాంతుడు, ఉంఛవృత్తి బ్రాహ్మణుడు సిద్ధుని గంగ గురించి అడగగా సిద్ధుడు ఆమె మహిమ చెబుతాడు. ఆమె జలం చల్లబడిన అన్ని జీవులు పరమ తృప్తి పొందుతాయని, ఆకాశం నుండి పడే గంగను శివుడు తలపై ధరించాడని అంటాడు.","ta":"கற்றறிந்த அமைதியான உஞ்சவிருத்தி அந்தணன் சித்தரிடம் கங்கை பற்றிக் கேட்க, சித்தர் அவள் பெருமையைக் கூறுகிறார். அவள் நீர் தெளிக்கப்பட்ட எல்லா உயிர்களும் உயர்ந்த நிறைவு பெறுகின்றன, வானிலிருந்து விழும் கங்கையைச் சிவன் தலையில் தாங்கினார் என்கிறார்.","ml":"പണ്ഡിതനും ശാന്തനുമായ ഒരു ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ, കതിർ പെറുക്കി ജീവിക്കുമ്പോൾ ഒരു സിദ്ധനോട് ഗംഗയെക്കുറിച്ച് ചോദിക്കുന്ന കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; സിദ്ധൻ അവളുടെ മഹത്ത്വം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. അവളുടെ ജലം തളിക്കപ്പെടുന്ന സകല ജീവികളും പരമശാന്തി നേടുമെന്നും, സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിൽനിന്ന് വീഴുന്ന ഗംഗയെ ശിവൻ തലയിൽ താങ്ങിയെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.27; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"बृहस्पतिसमं बुद्ध्या क्षमया ब्रह्मणः समम् ।\nपराक्रमे शक्रसममादित्यसमतेजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Equal to Brihaspati in intellect, equal to Brahma in patience, equal to Indra in valor and to the sun in radiance,"}},{"n":2,"text":"गाङ्गेयमर्जुनेनाजौ निहतं भूरिवर्चसम् ।\nभ्रातृभिः सहितोऽन्यैश्च पर्युपास्ते युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the very brilliant son of Ganga, struck down in battle by Arjuna, was attended by Yudhishthira together with his brothers and others."}},{"n":3,"text":"शयानं वीरशयने कालाकाङ्क्षिणमच्युतम् ।\nआजग्मुर्भरतश्रेष्ठं द्रष्टुकामा महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the undiminished best of the Bharatas lay on his bed of heroes awaiting the proper time, great sages came wishing to see him."}},{"n":4,"text":"अत्रिर्वसिष्ठोऽथ भृगुः पुलस्त्यः पुलहः क्रतुः ।\nअङ्गिरा गौतमोऽगस्त्यः सुमतिः स्वायुरात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Atri, Vasishtha, Bhrigu, Pulastya, Pulaha, Kratu, Angiras, Gautama, Agastya, Sumati, and the self-possessed Svayu,"}},{"n":5,"text":"विश्वामित्रः स्थूलशिराः संवर्तः प्रमतिर्दमः ।\nउशना बृहस्पतिर्व्यासश्च्यवनः काश्यपो ध्रुवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishvamitra, Sthulashiras, Samvarta, Pramati, Dama, Ushanas, Brihaspati, Vyasa, Chyavana, Kashyapa and Dhruva,"}},{"n":6,"text":"दुर्वासा जमदग्निश्च मार्कण्डेयोऽथ गालवः ।\nभरद्वाजश्च रैभ्यश्च यवक्रीतस्त्रितस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Durvasa, Jamadagni, Markandeya, Galava, Bharadvaja, Raibhya, Yavakrita and Trita,"}},{"n":7,"text":"स्थूलाक्षः शकलाक्षश्च कण्वो मेधातिथिः कृशः ।\nनारदः पर्वतश्चैव सुधन्वाथैकतो द्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sthulaksha, Shakalaksha, Kanva, Medhatithi, Krisha, Narada, Parvata, Sudhanva, Ekata and Dvita,"}},{"n":8,"text":"नितंभूर्भुवनो धौम्यः शतानन्दोऽकृतव्रणः ।\nजामदग्न्यस्तथा रामः काम्यश्चेत्येवमादयः ।\nसमागता महात्मानो भीष्मं द्रष्टुं महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nitambhu, Bhuvana, Dhaumya, Shatananda, Akritavrana, Rama son of Jamadagni, and Kamya and others: these great-souled great sages came to see Bhishma."}},{"n":9,"text":"तेषां महात्मनां पूजामागतानां युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभ्रातृभिः सहितश्चक्रे यथावदनुपूर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, with his brothers, honored those great-souled arrivals in due order as was proper."}},{"n":10,"text":"ते पूजिताः सुखासीनाः कथाश्चक्रुर्महर्षयः ।\nभीष्माश्रिताः सुमधुराः सर्वेन्द्रियमनोहराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored and seated at ease, those great sages told stories centered on Bhishma, very sweet and delightful to all the senses and the mind."}},{"n":11,"text":"भीष्मस्तेषां कथाः श्रुत्वा ऋषीणां भावितात्मनाम् ।\nमेने दिविस्थमात्मानं तुष्ट्या परमया युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the tales of those sages of trained souls, Bhishma, filled with supreme contentment, felt as though he were in heaven."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्ते भीष्ममामन्त्र्य पाण्डवांश्च महर्षयः ।\nअन्तर्धानं गताः सर्वे सर्वेषामेव पश्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, taking leave of Bhishma and the Pandavas, all the great sages vanished while everyone looked on."}},{"n":13,"text":"तानृषीन्सुमहाभागानन्तर्धानगतानपि ।\nपाण्डवास्तुष्टुवुः सर्वे प्रणेमुश्च मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even after those very fortunate sages had vanished, all the Pandavas praised them and bowed again and again."}},{"n":14,"text":"प्रसन्नमनसः सर्वे गाङ्गेयं कुरुसत्तमाः ।\nउपतस्थुर्यथोद्यन्तमादित्यं मन्त्रकोविदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With glad hearts, all the best of the Kurus attended the son of Ganga as those who know mantras attend the rising sun."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रभावात्तपसस्तेषामृषीणां वीक्ष्य पाण्डवाः ।\nप्रकाशन्तो दिशः सर्वा विस्मयं परमं ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the glory of those sages' austerity, which lit up all directions, the Pandavas were greatly amazed."}},{"n":16,"text":"महाभाग्यं परं तेषामृषीणामनुचिन्त्य ते ।\nपाण्डवाः सह भीष्मेण कथाश्चक्रुस्तदाश्रयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reflecting on the supreme good fortune of those sages, the Pandavas with Bhishma conversed on that theme."}},{"n":17,"text":"कथान्ते शिरसा पादौ स्पृष्ट्वा भीष्मस्य पाण्डवः ।\nधर्म्यं धर्मसुतः प्रश्नं पर्यपृच्छद्युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the talk, the Pandava Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, touched Bhishma's feet with his head and asked a question about dharma."}},{"n":18,"text":"के देशाः के जनपदा आश्रमाः के च पर्वताः ।\nप्रकृष्टाः पुण्यतः काश्च ज्ञेया नद्यः पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Grandfather, what regions, what countries, what hermitages and what mountains, and which rivers, are to be known as most excellent in merit?'"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nशिलोञ्छवृत्तेः संवादं सिद्धस्य च युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this too they cite an ancient tale, the conversation of a man living on gleaned grain and a Siddha, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":20,"text":"इमां कश्चित्परिक्रम्य पृथिवीं शैलभूषिताम् ।\nअसकृद्द्विपदां श्रेष्ठः श्रेष्ठस्य गृहमेधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A certain best of men, having roamed this earth adorned with mountains many times, came to the house of an excellent householder who lived on gleaned grain."}},{"n":21,"text":"शिलवृत्तेर्गृहं प्राप्तः स तेन विधिनार्चितः ।\nकृतकृत्य उपातिष्ठत्सिद्धं तमतिथिं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was honored by him in due form, and the contented householder attended on that Siddha guest."}},{"n":22,"text":"तौ समेत्य महात्मानौ सुखासीनौ कथाः शुभाः ।\nचक्रतुर्वेदसंबद्धास्तच्छेषकृतलक्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting, those two great-souled ones sat at ease and told auspicious stories connected with the Vedas, which marked the remainder of the day."}},{"n":23,"text":"शिलवृत्तिः कथान्ते तु सिद्धमामन्त्र्य यत्नतः ।\nप्रश्नं पप्रच्छ मेधावी यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the talk, the wise gleaner, carefully addressing the Siddha, asked the question that you now ask me."}},{"text":"शिलवृत्तिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The gleaner said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"के देशाः के जनपदाः केऽऽश्रमाः के च पर्वताः ।\nप्रकृष्टाः पुण्यतः काश्च ज्ञेया नद्यस्तदुच्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What regions, what countries, what hermitages and what mountains, and which rivers, are to be known as foremost in merit? Please tell me."}},{"text":"सिद्ध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Siddha said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"ते देशास्ते जनपदास्तेऽऽश्रमास्ते च पर्वताः ।\nयेषां भागीरथी गङ्गा मध्येनैति सरिद्वरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those are the regions, countries, hermitages and mountains through whose midst the Bhagirathi Ganga, best of rivers, flows."}},{"n":26,"text":"तपसा ब्रह्मचर्येण यज्ञैस्त्यागेन वा पुनः ।\nगतिं तां न लभेज्जन्तुर्गङ्गां संसेव्य यां लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By austerity, celibacy, sacrifices or renunciation, a creature cannot gain the goal that he gains by serving the Ganga."}},{"n":27,"text":"स्पृष्टानि येषां गाङ्गेयैस्तोयैर्गात्राणि देहिनाम् ।\nन्यस्तानि न पुनस्तेषां त्यागः स्वर्गाद्विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embodied beings whose bodies are touched by the Ganga's waters are never again made to give up heaven."}},{"n":28,"text":"सर्वाणि येषां गाङ्गेयैस्तोयैः कृत्यानि देहिनाम् ।\nगां त्यक्त्वा मानवा विप्र दिवि तिष्ठन्ति तेऽचलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, men for whom all rites are done with the Ganga's waters abide unshaken in heaven after leaving the earth."}},{"n":29,"text":"पूर्वे वयसि कर्माणि कृत्वा पापानि ये नराः ।\nपश्चाद्गङ्गां निषेवन्ते तेऽपि यान्त्युत्तमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even men who did sinful deeds in their early years and later serve the Ganga reach the highest goal."}},{"n":30,"text":"स्नातानां शुचिभिस्तोयैर्गाङ्गेयैः प्रयतात्मनाम् ।\nव्युष्टिर्भवति या पुंसां न सा क्रतुशतैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The merit that comes to purified, bathed men from the pure waters of the Ganga does not come even from hundreds of sacrifices."}},{"n":31,"text":"यावदस्थि मनुष्यस्य गङ्गातोयेषु तिष्ठति ।\nतावद्वर्षसहस्राणि स्वर्गं प्राप्य महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As long as a man's bone remains in the Ganga's waters, so many thousands of years he is honored after reaching heaven."}},{"n":32,"text":"अपहत्य तमस्तीव्रं यथा भात्युदये रविः ।\nतथापहत्य पाप्मानं भाति गङ्गाजलोक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sun at its rising shines after dispelling thick darkness, so one sprinkled with Ganga water shines after dispelling sin."}},{"n":33,"text":"विसोमा इव शर्वर्यो विपुष्पास्तरवो यथा ।\nतद्वद्देशा दिशश्चैव हीना गङ्गाजलैः शुभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like nights without the moon and trees without flowers, so are regions and directions without the Ganga's auspicious waters."}},{"n":34,"text":"वर्णाश्रमा यथा सर्वे स्वधर्मज्ञानवर्जिताः ।\nक्रतवश्च यथासोमास्तथा गङ्गां विना जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As all the stages of life without knowledge of one's own dharma, and as sacrifices without soma, so is the world without the Ganga."}},{"n":35,"text":"यथा हीनं नभोऽर्केण भूः शैलैः खं च वायुना ।\nतथा देशा दिशश्चैव गङ्गाहीना न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sky without the sun, the earth without mountains, and space without wind, so are regions and directions without the Ganga, without doubt."}},{"n":36,"text":"त्रिषु लोकेषु ये केचित्प्राणिनः सर्व एव ते ।\nतर्प्यमाणाः परां तृप्तिं यान्ति गङ्गाजलैः शुभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the beings in the three worlds, when given water of the Ganga's good waters, reach supreme satisfaction."}},{"n":37,"text":"यस्तु सूर्येण निष्टप्तं गाङ्गेयं पिबते जलम् ।\nगवां निर्हारनिर्मुक्ताद्यावकात्तद्विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who drinks Ganga water heated by the sun is better than one who lives on barley extracted from cow dung."}},{"n":38,"text":"इन्दुव्रतसहस्रं तु चरेद्यः कायशोधनम् ।\nपिबेद्यश्चापि गङ्गाम्भः समौ स्यातां न वा समौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who practices a thousand lunar vows to purify the body and one who drinks Ganga water: they are equal, or they are not equal."}},{"n":39,"text":"तिष्ठेद्युगसहस्रं तु पादेनैकेन यः पुमान् ।\nमासमेकं तु गङ्गायां समौ स्यातां न वा समौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who stands a thousand ages on one foot and one who spends one month in the Ganga: they are equal, or they are not equal."}},{"n":40,"text":"लम्बेतावाक्शिरा यस्तु युगानामयुतं पुमान् ।\nतिष्ठेद्यथेष्टं यश्चापि गङ्गायां स विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who hangs head down for ten thousand ages and one who stays in the Ganga as he likes: the latter is superior."}},{"n":41,"text":"अग्नौ प्राप्तं प्रधूयेत यथा तूलं द्विजोत्तम ।\nतथा गङ्गावगाढस्य सर्वं पापं प्रधूयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As cotton thrown into fire is burned away, brahmin, so all sin of one who has immersed in the Ganga is shaken off."}},{"n":42,"text":"भूतानामिह सर्वेषां दुःखोपहतचेतसाम् ।\nगतिमन्वेषमाणानां न गङ्गासदृशी गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For all beings here whose minds are struck by sorrow and who are seeking a refuge, there is no refuge like the Ganga."}},{"n":43,"text":"भवन्ति निर्विषाः सर्पा यथा तार्क्ष्यस्य दर्शनात् ।\nगङ्गाया दर्शनात्तद्वत्सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As serpents become venomless at the sight of Tarkshya, so at the sight of the Ganga one is freed from all sins."}},{"n":44,"text":"अप्रतिष्ठाश्च ये केचिदधर्मशरणाश्च ये ।\nतेषां प्रतिष्ठा गङ्गेह शरणं शर्म वर्म च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who have no support and whose refuge is adharma, the Ganga here is support, refuge, shelter and armor."}},{"n":45,"text":"प्रकृष्टैरशुभैर्ग्रस्ताननेकैः पुरुषाधमान् ।\nपततो नरके गङ्गा संश्रितान्प्रेत्य तारयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Ganga saves, after death, those lowest of men gripped by many grievous evils and falling into hell who have taken refuge in her."}},{"n":46,"text":"ते संविभक्ता मुनिभिर्नूनं देवैः सवासवैः ।\nयेऽभिगच्छन्ति सततं गङ्गामभिगतां सुरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely those who constantly go to the Ganga, to whom the gods have gone, have been favored by the sages and the gods with Indra."}},{"n":47,"text":"विनयाचारहीनाश्च अशिवाश्च नराधमाः ।\nते भवन्ति शिवा विप्र ये वै गङ्गां समाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the lowest of men, lacking humility and good conduct and inauspicious, become auspicious, brahmin, if they take refuge in the Ganga."}},{"n":48,"text":"यथा सुराणाममृतं पितॄणां च यथा स्वधा ।\nसुधा यथा च नागानां तथा गङ्गाजलं नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As nectar is for the gods, svadha for the ancestors and ambrosia for the nagas, so is Ganga water for men."}},{"n":49,"text":"उपासते यथा बाला मातरं क्षुधयार्दिताः ।\nश्रेयस्कामास्तथा गङ्गामुपासन्तीह देहिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As hungry children turn to their mother, so embodied beings who seek good turn to the Ganga here."}},{"n":50,"text":"स्वायंभुवं यथा स्थानं सर्वेषां श्रेष्ठमुच्यते ।\nस्नातानां सरितां श्रेष्ठा गङ्गा तद्वदिहोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Self-born's place is called the best of all, so the Ganga is called the best of rivers for those who bathe."}},{"n":51,"text":"यथोपजीविनां धेनुर्देवादीनां धरा स्मृता ।\nतथोपजीविनां गङ्गा सर्वप्राणभृतामिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the cow is said to be for those who live on her and the earth for gods and others, so the Ganga is for all who here live on her."}},{"n":52,"text":"देवाः सोमार्कसंस्थानि यथा सत्रादिभिर्मखैः ।\nअमृतान्युपजीवन्ति तथा गङ्गाजलं नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the gods live on the nectars in the moon and sun through sacrifices like long sessions, so people live on Ganga water."}},{"n":53,"text":"जाह्नवीपुलिनोत्थाभिः सिकताभिः समुक्षितः ।\nमन्यते पुरुषोऽऽत्मानं दिविष्ठमिव शोभितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man sprinkled with sands from the Jahnavi's bank thinks himself adorned as if standing in heaven."}},{"n":54,"text":"जाह्नवीतीरसंभूतां मृदं मूर्ध्ना बिभर्ति यः ।\nबिभर्ति रूपं सोऽर्कस्य तमोनाशात्सुनिर्मलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who carries clay from the Jahnavi's bank on his head carries the spotless form of the sun, because it destroys darkness."}},{"n":55,"text":"गङ्गोर्मिभिरथो दिग्धः पुरुषं पवनो यदा ।\nस्पृशते सोऽपि पाप्मानं सद्य एवापमार्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When wind, touched by the Ganga's waves, touches a man, it too wipes away his sin at once."}},{"n":56,"text":"व्यसनैरभितप्तस्य नरस्य विनशिष्यतः ।\nगङ्गादर्शनजा प्रीतिर्व्यसनान्यपकर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The joy born of seeing the Ganga removes the troubles of a man who is scorched by calamities and about to perish."}},{"n":57,"text":"हंसारावैः कोकरवै रवैरन्यैश्च पक्षिणाम् ।\nपस्पर्ध गङ्गा गन्धर्वान्पुलिनैश्च शिलोच्चयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the cries of swans and chakravakas and the other calls of birds, and with her banks, the Ganga rivaled the gandharvas and mountain heights."}},{"n":58,"text":"हंसादिभिः सुबहुभिर्विविधैः पक्षिभिर्वृताम् ।\nगङ्गां गोकुलसंबाधां दृष्ट्वा स्वर्गोऽपि विस्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Ganga surrounded by many kinds of birds such as swans, and crowded with herds of cattle, one forgets even heaven."}},{"n":59,"text":"न सा प्रीतिर्दिविष्ठस्य सर्वकामानुपाश्नतः ।\nअभवद्या परा प्रीतिर्गङ्गायाः पुलिने नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The supreme joy that men find on the Ganga's bank is not matched even by one in heaven who enjoys all desires."}},{"n":60,"text":"वाङ्मनःकर्मजैर्ग्रस्तः पापैरपि पुमानिह ।\nवीक्ष्य गङ्गां भवेत्पूतस्तत्र मे नास्ति संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a man seized by sins of speech, mind and action becomes pure upon seeing the Ganga; about that I have no doubt."}},{"n":61,"text":"सप्तावरान्सप्त परान्पितॄंस्तेभ्यश्च ये परे ।\nपुमांस्तारयते गङ्गां वीक्ष्य स्पृष्ट्वावगाह्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing, touching and bathing in the Ganga, a man rescues seven ancestors before and seven after, and those beyond them."}},{"n":62,"text":"श्रुताभिलषिता दृष्टा स्पृष्टा पीतावगाहिता ।\nगङ्गा तारयते नॄणामुभौ वंशौ विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heard, desired, seen, touched, drunk and bathed in, the Ganga rescues people, especially both their lineages."}},{"n":63,"text":"दर्शनात्स्पर्शनात्पानात्तथा गङ्गेति कीर्तनात् ।\nपुनात्यपुण्यान्पुरुषाञ्शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By seeing, touching, drinking and by uttering 'Ganga,' she purifies sinful men by hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":64,"text":"य इच्छेत्सफलं जन्म जीवितं श्रुतमेव च ।\nस पितॄंस्तर्पयेद्गङ्गामभिगम्य सुरांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who wants his birth, life and learning to bear fruit should go to the Ganga and satisfy his ancestors and the gods."}},{"n":65,"text":"न सुतैर्न च वित्तेन कर्मणा न च तत्फलम् ।\nप्राप्नुयात्पुरुषोऽत्यन्तं गङ्गां प्राप्य यदाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man cannot gain through sons, wealth or rites that fruit that he fully gains on reaching the Ganga."}},{"n":66,"text":"जात्यन्धैरिह तुल्यास्ते मृतैः पङ्गुभिरेव च ।\nसमर्था ये न पश्यन्ति गङ्गां पुण्यजलां शिवाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are able but do not see the Ganga, the holy-watered and auspicious, are like those blind from birth, dead, or lame."}},{"n":67,"text":"भूतभव्यभविष्यज्ञैर्महर्षिभिरुपस्थिताम् ।\nदेवैः सेन्द्रैश्च को गङ्गां नोपसेवेत मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man would not serve the Ganga, attended by great sages who know past, present and future, and by the gods with Indra?"}},{"n":68,"text":"वानप्रस्थैर्गृहस्थैश्च यतिभिर्ब्रह्मचारिभिः ।\nविद्यावद्भिः श्रितां गङ्गां पुमान्को नाम नाश्रयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man would not take refuge in the Ganga, resorted to by forest-dwellers, householders, ascetics, celibates and the learned?"}},{"n":69,"text":"उत्क्रामद्भिश्च यः प्राणैः प्रयतः शिष्टसंमतः ।\nचिन्तयेन्मनसा गङ्गां स गतिं परमां लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A restrained man, approved by the good, who thinks of the Ganga in his mind as his breaths depart obtains the highest goal."}},{"n":70,"text":"न भयेभ्यो भयं तस्य न पापेभ्यो न राजतः ।\nआ देहपतनाद्गङ्गामुपास्ते यः पुमानिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a man here who serves the Ganga until his body falls, there is no fear from dangers, sins or kings."}},{"n":71,"text":"गगनाद्यां महापुण्यां पतन्तीं वै महेश्वरः ।\nदधार शिरसा देवीं तामेव दिवि सेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great Maheshvara bore on his head that very holy goddess as she fell from the sky, and he attends her in heaven."}},{"n":72,"text":"अलंकृतास्त्रयो लोकाः पथिभिर्विमलैस्त्रिभिः ।\nयस्तु तस्या जलं सेवेत्कृतकृत्यः पुमान्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The three worlds are adorned by her three pure paths; a man who uses her water becomes one whose work is done."}},{"n":73,"text":"दिवि ज्योतिर्यथादित्यः पितॄणां चैव चन्द्रमाः ।\nदेवेशश्च यथा नॄणां गङ्गेह सरितां तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sun is the light in the sky, the moon for the ancestors and the lord of gods for men, so is the Ganga among rivers here."}},{"n":74,"text":"मात्रा पित्रा सुतैर्दारैर्वियुक्तस्य धनेन वा ।\nन भवेद्धि तथा दुःखं यथा गङ्गावियोगजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man separated from mother, father, sons, wives or wealth does not suffer as he does from separation from the Ganga."}},{"n":75,"text":"नारण्यैर्नेष्टविषयैर्न सुतैर्न धनागमैः ।\nतथा प्रसादो भवति गङ्गां वीक्ष्य यथा नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither forests, nor desired objects, nor sons, nor gain of wealth gives people such joy as seeing the Ganga."}},{"n":76,"text":"पूर्णमिन्दुं यथा दृष्ट्वा नृणां दृष्टिः प्रसीदति ।\nगङ्गां त्रिपथगां दृष्ट्वा तथा दृष्टिः प्रसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sight of the full moon brightens people's eyes, so the sight of the three-pathed Ganga brightens the eye."}},{"n":77,"text":"तद्भावस्तद्गतमनास्तन्निष्ठस्तत्परायणः ।\nगङ्गां योऽनुगतो भक्त्या स तस्याः प्रियतां व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who follows the Ganga with devotion, his mind absorbed in her, intent on her and relying on her, becomes dear to her."}},{"n":78,"text":"भूःस्थैः खस्थैर्दिविष्ठैश्च भूतैरुच्चावचैरपि ।\nगङ्गा विगाह्या सततमेतत्कार्यतमं सताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beings on earth, in the sky and in heaven, high and low, should always plunge into the Ganga; this is the most important duty of the good."}},{"n":79,"text":"त्रिषु लोकेषु पुण्यत्वाद्गङ्गायाः प्रथितं यशः ।\nयत्पुत्रान्सगरस्यैषा भस्माख्याननयद्दिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Ganga's fame for holiness is widespread in the three worlds, since she took the ashes of Sagara's sons to heaven."}},{"n":80,"text":"वाय्वीरिताभिः सुमहास्वनाभि-\nर्द्रुताभिरत्यर्थसमुच्छ्रिताभिः ।\nगङ्गोर्मिभिर्भानुमतीभिरिद्धः\nसहस्ररश्मिप्रतिमो विभाति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lit by Ganga's waves, which are driven by the wind, loud, swift, rising high and sun-bright, he shines like the thousand-rayed sun."}},{"n":81,"text":"पयस्विनीं घृतिनीमत्युदारां\nसमृद्धिनीं वेगिनीं दुर्विगाह्याम् ।\nगङ्गां गत्वा यैः शरीरं विसृष्टं\nगता धीरास्ते विबुधैः समत्वम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who, having gone to the Ganga, rich in water and in ghee, very generous, prosperous, swift and hard to plunge into, gave up their bodies there, those steady ones attained equality with the gods."}},{"n":82,"text":"अन्धाञ्जडान्द्रव्यहीनांश्च गङ्गा\nयशस्विनी बृहती विश्वरूपा ।\nदेवैः सेन्द्रैर्मुनिभिर्मानवैश्च\nनिषेविता सर्वकामैर्युनक्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The renowned, vast, many-formed Ganga, served by gods with Indra, sages and men, grants the blind, the dull and the poor all their desires."}},{"n":83,"text":"ऊर्जावतीं मधुमतीं महापुण्यां त्रिवर्त्मगाम् ।\nत्रिलोकगोप्त्रीं ये गङ्गां संश्रितास्ते दिवं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who take refuge in the Ganga, rich in strength and sweetness, greatly holy, going by three paths and guarding the three worlds, have gone to heaven."}},{"n":84,"text":"यो वत्स्यति द्रक्ष्यति वापि मर्त्य-\nस्तस्मै प्रयच्छन्ति सुखानि देवाः ।\nतद्भाविताः स्पर्शने दर्शने य-\nस्तस्मै देवा गतिमिष्टां दिशन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods give happiness to a mortal who will live by her or see her; and to the one who is devoted at her touch and sight, the gods grant the goal he wishes."}},{"n":85,"text":"दक्षां पृथ्वीं बृहतीं विप्रकृष्टां\nशिवामृतां सुरसां सुप्रसन्नाम् ।\nविभावरीं सर्वभूतप्रतिष्ठां\nगङ्गां गता ये त्रिदिवं गतास्ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who have gone to the Ganga, skilled, earthlike, vast, far-reaching, auspicious, immortal, sweet-flavored, very clear, the night-like, support of all beings, have gone to the third heaven."}},{"n":86,"text":"ख्यातिर्यस्याः खं दिवं गां च नित्यं\nपुरा दिशो विदिशश्चावतस्थे ।\nतस्या जलं सेव्य सरिद्वराया\nमर्त्याः सर्वे कृतकृत्या भवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Her fame has always spread through the sky, heaven, earth, directions and intermediate directions. Mortals who use the water of that best of rivers all become fulfilled."}},{"n":87,"text":"इयं गङ्गेति नियतं प्रतिष्ठा\nगुहस्य रुक्मस्य च गर्भयोषा ।\nप्रातस्त्रिमार्गा घृतवहा विपाप्मा\nगङ्गावतीर्णा वियतो विश्वतोया ॥","meaning":{"en":"'This is the Ganga'; she is the established support of Guha and of the golden one, womb-bearer; the three-pathed, ghee-bearing, sinless one, descended from the sky, with waters for all, shines each morning."}},{"n":88,"text":"सुतावनीध्रस्य हरस्य भार्या\nदिवो भुवश्चापि कक्ष्यानुरूपा ।\nभव्या पृथिव्या भाविनी भाति राज-\nन्गङ्गा लोकानां पुण्यदा वै त्रयाणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, the Ganga, wife of Hara, the mountain's daughter, suited to heaven and earth, who is blessed and destined for the earth, shines, giving merit to the three worlds."}},{"n":89,"text":"मधुप्रवाहा घृतरागोद्धृताभि-\nर्महोर्मिभिः शोभिता ब्राह्मणैश्च ।\nदिवश्च्युता शिरसात्ता भवेन\nगङ्गावनीध्रास्त्रिदिवस्य माला ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honey-flowing, adorned by great waves bearing the color of ghee and by brahmins, fallen from heaven and borne on his head, the Ganga is a garland of the third heaven for the mountains."}},{"n":90,"text":"योनिर्वरिष्ठा विरजा वितन्वी\nशुष्मा इरा वारिवहा यशोदा ।\nविश्वावती चाकृतिरिष्टिरिद्धा\nगङ्गोक्षितानां भुवनस्य पन्थाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is the best source, stainless, expansive, powerful, nourishing, bearing water, giving fame, all-sustaining, shape and offering, blazing; she is the path of the world for those sprinkled by the Ganga."}},{"n":91,"text":"क्षान्त्या मह्या गोपने धारणे च\nदीप्त्या कृशानोस्तपनस्य चैव ।\nतुल्या गङ्गा संमता ब्राह्मणानां\nगुहस्य ब्रह्मण्यतया च नित्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of her patience, her protecting and bearing the earth, and her brilliance like fire and the sun, the Ganga is considered equal to brahmins and always devoted to the priesthood like Guha."}},{"n":92,"text":"ऋषिष्टुतां विष्णुपदीं पुराणीं\nसुपुण्यतोयां मनसापि लोके ।\nसर्वात्मना जाह्नवीं ये प्रपन्ना-\nस्ते ब्रह्मणः सदनं संप्रयाताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who fully take refuge in the Jahnavi, praised by the sages, ancient, the foot of Vishnu, with greatly holy waters, even in thought in the world, have gone to Brahma's abode."}},{"n":93,"text":"लोकानिमान्नयति या जननीव पुत्रा-\nन्सर्वात्मना सर्वगुणोपपन्ना ।\nस्वस्थानमिष्टमिह ब्राह्ममभीप्समानै-\nर्गङ्गा सदैवात्मवशैरुपास्या ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Ganga, like a mother leading her sons to these worlds, endowed with all virtues, should always be served by those who master themselves and wish for their own place in Brahma's realm."}},{"n":94,"text":"उस्रां जुष्टां मिषतीं विश्वतोया-\nमिरां वज्रीं रेवतीं भूधराणाम् ।\nशिष्टाश्रयाममृतां ब्रह्मकान्तां\nगङ्गां श्रयेदात्मवान्सिद्धिकामः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is self-possessed and desires success should take refuge in the Ganga, the dawn-like, attended, shining, with waters for all, the earth's food, the wielder of the thunderbolt, rich, the supporter of mountains, refuge of the good, immortal and beloved of Brahma."}},{"n":95,"text":"प्रसाद्य देवान्सविभून्समस्ता-\nन्भगीरथस्तपसोग्रेण गङ्गाम् ।\nगामानयत्तामभिगम्य शश्व-\nन्पुमान्भयं नेह नामुत्र विद्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After propitiating all the gods and the powerful with fierce austerity, Bhagiratha brought the Ganga to earth; a man who always goes to her knows no fear here or hereafter."}},{"n":96,"text":"उदाहृतः सर्वथा ते गुणानां\nमयैकदेशः प्रसमीक्ष्य बुद्ध्या ।\nशक्तिर्न मे काचिदिहास्ति वक्तुं\nगुणान्सर्वान्परिमातुं तथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you only one part of her virtues, having considered with my mind; I have no power here to tell all her virtues or measure them."}},{"n":97,"text":"मेरोः समुद्रस्य च सर्वरत्नैः\nसंख्योपलानामुदकस्य वापि ।\nवक्तुं शक्यं नेह गङ्गाजलानां\nगुणाख्यानं परिमातुं तथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is not possible to tell or measure the qualities of Ganga's waters any more than one can tell the jewels of Meru and the ocean, the number of stones, or the water."}},{"n":98,"text":"तस्मादिमान्परया श्रद्धयोक्ता-\nन्गुणान्सर्वाञ्जाह्नवीजांस्तथैव ।\nभजेद्वाचा मनसा कर्मणा च\nभक्त्या युक्तः परया श्रद्दधानः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, with supreme faith one should honor with speech, mind and action all these qualities born of the Jahnavi that I have told, with devotion and belief."}},{"n":99,"text":"लोकानिमांस्त्रीन्यशसा वितत्य\nसिद्धिं प्राप्य महतीं तां दुरापाम् ।\nगङ्गाकृतानचिरेणैव लोका-\nन्यथेष्टमिष्टान्विचरिष्यसि त्वम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spread through the three worlds with fame and gained that great, hard-to-reach success, you will soon roam as you wish in the worlds made by the Ganga."}},{"n":100,"text":"तव मम च गुणैर्महानुभावा\nजुषतु मतिं सततं स्वधर्मयुक्तैः ।\nअभिगतजनवत्सला हि गङ्गा\nभजति युनक्ति सुखैश्च भक्तिमन्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"May the great-minded one, always devoted to his own duty, take pleasure in your and my qualities; for the Ganga is kind to those who approach her, and gives her devotee happiness and joins him to devotion."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":101,"text":"इति परममतिर्गुणाननेका-\nञ्शिलरतये त्रिपथानुयोगरूपान् ।\nबहुविधमनुशास्य तथ्यरूपा-\nन्गगनतलं द्युतिमान्विवेश सिद्धः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having taught the gleaner in many ways such many true qualities of the three-pathed Ganga, the radiant Siddha of supreme wisdom entered the sky."}},{"n":102,"text":"शिलवृत्तिस्तु सिद्धस्य वाक्यैः संबोधितस्तदा ।\nगङ्गामुपास्य विधिवत्सिद्धिं प्राप्तः सुदुर्लभाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the gleaner, awakened by the Siddha's words, served the Ganga properly and attained the success that is very hard to gain."}},{"n":103,"text":"तस्मात्त्वमपि कौन्तेय भक्त्या परमया युतः ।\nगङ्गामभ्येहि सततं प्राप्स्यसे सिद्धिमुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore you too, son of Kunti, filled with supreme devotion, should go to the Ganga constantly; you will gain the best success."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":104,"text":"श्रुत्वेतिहासं भीष्मोक्तं गङ्गायाः स्तवसंयुतम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरः परां प्रीतिमगच्छद्भ्रातृभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the tale told by Bhishma, with its praise of the Ganga, Yudhishthira and his brothers felt supreme joy."}},{"n":105,"text":"इतिहासमिमं पुण्यं शृणुयाद्यः पठेत वा ।\nगङ्गायाः स्तवसंयुक्तं स मुच्येत्सर्वकिल्बिषैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who hears or recites this holy tale, joined with the praise of the Ganga, is freed from all sins."}}]}]}